WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.060
Mean absolute error adds the
magnitude of every aligned residual,

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:08.540
preventing positive and
negative misses from cancelling.

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:10.520
For the selected model,

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:14.413
total absolute error is five
hundred and forty eight thousand,

00:00:14.413 --> 00:00:17.640
six hundred and ninety eight
point one one one nine.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.780
Dividing by four thousand,

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:24.387
three hundred and seventy five recorded
hours gives one hundred and twenty five

00:00:24.387 --> 00:00:27.490
point four one six seven rentals per hour.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:31.230
The denominator is the
observed evaluation population,

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:34.050
not every expected calendar slot.

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:37.570
This definition stayed fixed
before the test was opened,

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:41.310
so it can be compared honestly
with the prior validation score.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.770
Absolute error answers
average miss magnitude.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:51.170
Root mean squared error squares
each miss before averaging,

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.850
then takes the root to
return to rental units.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:57.550
Here it is one hundred and
seventy four point four seven.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:02.210
Mean signed error is negative one
hundred and eleven point three six,

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.790
showing substantial underprediction.

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:07.670
These numbers answer different questions.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:12.560
A near zero signed average could hide
equally large positive and negative

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:13.170
misses,

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:16.570
while squaring makes large
errors more influential.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:21.730
Keeping all three prevents one attractive
number from substituting for the task.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:26.880
None is a calibrated uncertainty interval
or a measure of downstream inventory

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:27.810
value.

00:01:29.837 --> 00:01:34.961
The group predictor won validation with
mean absolute error ninety one point five

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:39.447
seven, ahead of the retained forest
at ninety nine point eight three.

00:01:40.017 --> 00:01:40.607
Later,

00:01:40.617 --> 00:01:44.027
the group score rises to one hundred
and twenty five point four two,

00:01:44.257 --> 00:01:47.547
while the forest scores one
hundred and three point six five.

00:01:48.437 --> 00:01:51.917
Interaction regression also scores
below groups on the final hours,

00:01:51.917 --> 00:01:54.427
at one hundred and
eleven point three zero.

00:01:55.297 --> 00:01:59.787
All seven rows share the same final
membership and already selected policies.

00:02:00.437 --> 00:02:04.227
This is a real negative finding about
the original selection’s transfer.

00:02:04.737 --> 00:02:08.757
Hiding the reversal would make the
project easier to celebrate and harder to

00:02:08.757 --> 00:02:09.527
understand.

00:02:11.817 --> 00:02:14.987
The result comes from
row aligned forecasts.

00:02:15.577 --> 00:02:17.847
Each prediction carries the same record,

00:02:18.097 --> 00:02:21.007
target time and issue
time as its observation.

00:02:21.777 --> 00:02:23.767
The scorer refuses missing,

00:02:23.937 --> 00:02:27.727
duplicated or reordered
identities before reducing errors.

00:02:28.537 --> 00:02:31.424
Independent verification
checks all thirty thousand,

00:02:31.424 --> 00:02:34.507
six hundred and twenty
five final forecasts,

00:02:35.197 --> 00:02:36.127
the error arithmetic

00:02:36.777 --> 00:02:37.787
and the slice totals.

00:02:38.437 --> 00:02:42.237
Group predictions are also recomputed
directly from the original training

00:02:42.237 --> 00:02:42.887
observations.

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:48.187
Passing these checks establishes the
measured values and fixed execution,

00:02:48.557 --> 00:02:51.287
while a disappointing score
remains disappointing.

00:02:51.977 --> 00:02:55.507
Correct code and strong later
forecasting are separate conclusions.

00:02:57.983 --> 00:03:00.587
The group artifact uses five thousand,

00:03:00.587 --> 00:03:06.313
six hundred and forty JSON bytes, while
the forest uses about sixteen million.

00:03:06.723 --> 00:03:12.283
Historical fitting took about zero point
zero one three six seconds for groups and

00:03:12.283 --> 00:03:15.333
zero point six seven
six two for the forest.

00:03:16.163 --> 00:03:21.703
Final saved snapshot replay took roughly
zero point zero two eight eight and

00:03:21.703 --> 00:03:25.013
zero point one eight four two
seconds for the full batches.

00:03:25.743 --> 00:03:29.173
These costs belong to this local
implementation and machine.

00:03:29.603 --> 00:03:31.653
Storage bytes are not peak memory,

00:03:31.763 --> 00:03:36.653
and batch snapshot traversal is not
optimized per request production latency.

00:03:36.963 --> 00:03:41.673
Cost can inform another decision without
rewriting the fixed quality comparison.

00:03:44.067 --> 00:03:47.867
The application keeps the
original selected badge on groups,

00:03:47.867 --> 00:03:51.847
preserving the distinction between
the development decision and the final

00:03:51.847 --> 00:03:52.577
finding.

00:03:53.267 --> 00:03:56.717
This does not force deployment of
a model regardless of evidence.

00:03:57.207 --> 00:03:59.517
Choosing the forest
next can be reasonable,

00:03:59.787 --> 00:04:02.637
but the choice now uses
knowledge from this test.

00:04:03.047 --> 00:04:06.997
A new independent performance
claim needs new held out evidence.

00:04:07.347 --> 00:04:12.907
The task also never supplied an
operational error threshold or the cost of

00:04:12.907 --> 00:04:15.157
missed demand versus idle bicycles.

00:04:15.887 --> 00:04:19.557
Beating a global mean therefore does
not establish planning readiness.

00:04:20.567 --> 00:04:23.297
The result supports a more
informed next conversation,

00:04:23.707 --> 00:04:25.617
not an invented acceptance gate.

